---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Poesis is the company harnessing the generative AI era so that systems continuously develop on their own — created by Clément Cazaud."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="motto">Define the world in software; generate it.</p>
      <h1>We make definitions generate systems.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Poesis transforms organizations — IT first — through AI-generative, agentic capabilities grounded in systemic governance. We author the open standard, build the engine and application that run it, and deliver the transformation around them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our mission</p>
      <h2>Governance that systems can act on.</h2>
      <p class="lead">The governance definitions organizations should build from &mdash; and evaluate against &mdash; have always lived in prose, scattered across wikis, compliance spreadsheets, and review boards that drift from reality. Our mission is to turn them into typed, versioned, machine-operable definitions, and to ship the <a href="/sie">engine</a> and <a href="/itip">applications</a> that contextualize and harness generative AI &mdash; bringing forth, for the first time in history, genuinely synthetic autopoietic systems to our civilization.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Team</p>
      <h2>The people behind Poesis.</h2>
      <p class="lead">The <a href="/standard">GSM</a> standard, <a href="/sie">SIE</a>, and <a href="/itip">ITIP</a> originate from a single thesis: systems should be programatically <em>defined and governed</em>, not merely prosed. That project is carried by three persons.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1.6rem">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="founder-head">
            <img class="founder-avatar" src="/clement-cazaud.jpg" alt="Portrait of Clément Cazaud" width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <span class="tag">Founder</span>
              <h3>Clément Cazaud</h3>
              <p class="title">Chief Executive Officier</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Enterprise &amp; solutions architect, software engineer, agentic AI expert, and systems thinker. Clément has spent his career turning sprawling IT landscapes into coherent, governed systems: mapping architectures, leading transformations, and building the tooling that makes governance executable rather than aspirational. GSM, SIE, and ITIP grew out of that work &mdash; and out of the agentic AI era that now makes it tractable: the conviction that the definitions a system must obey belong in software, where they can be versioned, reasoned over, and generated from.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:.6rem"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/clement-cazaud" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the full track record on LinkedIn →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="founder-head">
            <img class="founder-avatar" src="/brahim-ben-helal.jpg" alt="Portrait of Brahim Ben Helal" width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <span class="tag">Co-Founder</span>
              <h3>Brahim Ben Helal</h3>
              <p class="title">Chief Growth Officer</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Brahim has spent his career bridging technology and business, helping enterprise software companies transform complex platforms into scalable commercial success. Combining deep experience in SaaS, AI, digital trust, and enterprise sales, he specializes in designing go-to-market strategies, product positioning, and commercial systems that accelerate adoption while aligning product innovation with market demand.</p>
          <p>At Poesis, he leads growth strategy, ecosystem development, and customer engagement, working alongside product and engineering to ensure the platform addresses real-world enterprise challenges. His focus is on making advanced AI systems understandable, adoptable, and commercially impactful, helping organizations move from experimentation to governed, scalable deployment.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:.6rem"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brahim-ben-helal-50273856" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the full track record on LinkedIn →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1.6rem"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact">Get in touch →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .founder-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .founder-avatar {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 72px;
    height: 72px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(45, 212, 191, .12);
  }
  .founder-head .tag + h3 {
    margin-top: .5rem;
  }
</style>

